   ('Introducing Claude Opus 5','https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5','product','2026-07-24','Anthropic released Opus 5 as a flagship for long-running agents, emphasizing verification, iteration, coding, automation, and adjustable effort.','Use it to test difficult Buildn/client tasks where a self-checking agent could replace repeated human re-prompting: migrations, debugging, research synthesis, and browser verification.','Vendor benchmarks and early-access accounts are directional, not proof for local workloads.','Define one hard task, a pass/fail rubric, a cost cap, and a control model before a trial.'),
   ('Claude Opus 5 Now Available in GitHub Copilot','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-24-claude-opus-5-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/','release','2026-07-24','GitHub is gradually exposing Opus 5 across Copilot surfaces for Pro+, Max, Business, and Enterprise; managed plans require an admin policy toggle.','Run the same bounded code task through a familiar Copilot surface before changing any agent harness or developer workflow.','Cybersecurity-adjacent prompts can be blocked; plan a model fallback rather than assuming uniform tool behavior.','Enable it for a small pilot group and compare merged, tested outcomes—not chat satisfaction.'),
   ('Claude Platform release notes — July 24','https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview','docs','2026-07-24','The API release adds claude-opus-5 with 1M context and effort tiers, allows mid-conversation tool changes in beta, and removes Opus 4.7 fast mode.','Audit direct API callers for speed=fast, then use effort as a deliberate quality/cost dial in a test harness.','At xhigh and max, thinking cannot be disabled; workloads must accept that behavior and cost profile.','Search production configuration for claude-opus-4-7 plus speed=fast today.'),
