   ('OKF v0.2 adds trust signals','https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/okf-v0-2-adds-trust-signals/','blog','2026-07-24','Google’s Open Knowledge Format v0.2 adds optional provenance, generated/verified, stale_after, status, and attestation vocabulary to Markdown/YAML knowledge bundles.','Create a small Buildn project-context bundle for one client: canonical metrics, runbooks, ownership, source links, and a re-verification date.','The format records signals rather than enforcing policy; consumers still need rules for what they may trust or execute.','Prototype three files: a metric, a runbook, and a client constraint with stale_after dates.'),
   ('Open Knowledge Format reference implementation','https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/tree/main/okf','repo','2026-07-24','The public reference repository provides the concrete spec, samples, and tooling context behind OKF rather than leaving the trust model as a blog concept.','Use it to keep agent-readable context portable across tools instead of embedding key operating facts in a single vendor workspace.','A reference implementation is not a substitute for source-of-truth ownership or access control.','Fork nothing yet; inspect the sample bundle and map it to one existing project folder.'),
